<resources>
    <string name="game_setup_rules_standard_1">Everyone starts with 501 points (or 101, 301, 701 or a custom score). Each turn you throw three darts and their sum is subtracted.</string>
    <string name="game_setup_rules_standard_2">The first to reach exactly 0 wins the leg. With Double Out the last dart must be a double; with Double In scoring only starts with the first double.</string>
    <string name="game_setup_rules_standard_3">Going below 0 (with Double Out also to 1) is a bust: the turn doesn't count.</string>
    <string name="game_setup_rules_cricket_1">Only 15 to 20 and the Bull count. Each number is closed after three hits; a double counts twice, a triple three times, on the Bull a single counts once and a double twice.</string>
    <string name="game_setup_rules_cricket_2">Further hits on one of your closed numbers that an opponent still has open score points.</string>
    <string name="game_setup_rules_cricket_3">The leg ends when everyone has closed everything. Standard: you score the points yourself, the most points win. Cut Throat: the points go to your opponents, the fewest points win.</string>
    <string name="game_setup_rules_all_fives_1">A turn only counts if all three darts hit and their sum is divisible by 5. The whole sum is then credited.</string>
    <string name="game_setup_rules_all_fives_2">The first to reach the target score (50, 75 or 100) wins the leg.</string>
    <string name="game_setup_rules_atc_1">Hit the numbers in order from 1 to 20, optionally backwards or with the Bull at the end. The first to finish wins.</string>
    <string name="game_setup_rules_atc_2">Standard: every segment of the number counts. Doubles / Triples: only that segment counts.</string>
    <string name="game_setup_rules_atc_3">Quickly: single, double and triple advance you 1, 2 or 3 numbers. Shanghai: hit single, double and triple in turn on each number.</string>
